0.00_00  2026-11-12  UNTAGGED
    [ This version is entirely generated. ]

    + RdKw::L10N::Utf8TextDomain: __, __n and N__ of a text domain,
      put in the package that uses it: the domain and its
      LOCALEDIR given (use ... DOMAIN[, LOCALEDIR]), or as a module
      says ($DOMAIN and $LOCALEDIR of use ... ':module' => MODULE;
      none, if it cannot be loaded).  As RdKw::WwW::GenGenLib 0.01_00
      had them: messages are characters, the domain is bound to
      UTF-8, and both ways are strict; as they are written, without
      Locale::Messages (libintl-perl); and $! (and $^E) as they were
      after them, for a %m.  Nothing but what comes with Perl.
